  "preamble": "Fortition and lateralization of a rhotic to the voiceless lateral fricative [ɬ] turns an alveolar trill into a lateral with turbulent airflow. Thao, a nearly extinct Formosan language of Sun Moon Lake, has ɬ, written ⟨lh⟩, as the regular reflex of Proto-Austronesian *R, which Blust reconstructs as an alveolar trill: *RaməC 'root' became lhamic and *busuR 'bow' became futulh. Other Formosan languages have l (Bunun busul) or lose it (Paiwan umaq 'house' from *Rumaq).",
